# ActaNex Open — Release & Version Sync

## Source of truth

- Canonical app version is root `package.json` → `"version"`.
- Keep in lockstep on every GA bump:
  - `package.json` / `package-lock.json` (root + `packages[""].version`)
  - `src/Worker/package.json` / `src/Worker/package-lock.json`
  - `CHANGELOG.md` section `## [x.y.z]`
  - UI fallbacks: `src/Web/views/settings.html` (`data-app-version`), `src/Web/release-notes.html`, `src/Worker/src/templates/release_notes_page.ts`
  - Release artifacts after `npm run build:release`: `src/Worker/bundle/worker.bundle.js`, `src/Worker/bundle/update-release.json` (must contain the same `version`)
- Never ship a GitHub Release / tag whose `package.json` disagrees with Worker package / CHANGELOG / `update-release.json`.

## Dual checkouts (mandatory awareness)

There are commonly **two clones**:

| Checkout | Typical path |
| :--- | :--- |
| Cursor / Projects | `C:\Users\Micha\Projects\actanex-open` |
| OneDrive (Hub docs reference) | `C:\Users\Micha\OneDrive\Dokumente\AI-Projects\ActaNex-Open` |

Before stating “current version”, run `git branch --show-current` and read `package.json` in **the checkout you are editing**. Do not assume Projects `main` matches OneDrive `CF-instance-update`.

After any release commit/tag/push:

1. Fast-forward **both** checkouts to the release branch tip (and `main` after merge).
2. Confirm both report the same `package.json` / Worker / `update-release.json` version.
3. Leave unrelated untracked docs (e.g. solution-design drafts) alone unless asked.

## Branch & publish flow

1. Develop / release on `CF-instance-update` (or agreed release branch).
2. Bump versions + CHANGELOG + release-notes UI **in one commit**.
3. `npm install` (root + `src/Worker` if needed) → `npm run build:release` → `npm test`.
4. Commit artifacts with the version bump.
5. Annotated tag `vx.y.z`, push branch + tag.
6. `gh release create` with `worker.bundle.js` and `update-release.json` assets.
7. Open PR **release branch → `main`**, merge promptly so Projects/`main` does not stay on an older GA.
8. Update **Platform Hub** in the same session (or immediately after):
   - `wrangler.inbound.toml` `DEFAULT_RELEASE_VERSION = "vx.y.z"`
   - Code fallbacks (`constants`, provisioning, github API empty fallback, portal/admin selects)
   - Copy Open `worker.bundle.js` → Hub `src/customer-template/bundle/worker.bundle.js`
   - Hub `docs/RELEASE_NOTES.md` + build changelog step
9. Hub deploy of inbound vars / Flotten-Rollout is a separate ops step; still update the **pointers** in git.

## Hygiene / empty content releases

If a prior tag was published with incomplete hygiene (missing CHANGELOG section, Worker package behind root, `main` not merged):

- Prefer a new patch (e.g. `x.y.(z+1)`) with **no functional app changes** over rewriting a published tag.
- Document the gap in CHANGELOG for both the incomplete GA and the hygiene patch.

## What Hub deploys do **not** do

Hub commits that only change `DEFAULT_RELEASE_VERSION` do **not** bump Open `package.json`. Never claim Open advanced solely because Hub was deployed.

## Verification checklist (agent must run)

```text
node -e "console.log(require('./package.json').version, require('./src/Worker/package.json').version, require('./src/Worker/bundle/update-release.json').version)"
git branch --show-current
gh release view vX.Y.Z --json tagName,assets
```

All three version strings must match; release assets must include both bundle files; `main` should contain the release after the merge PR.
